<configs>
<!--
  Armory Unbound - perk parts. One part per perk; property AuPerk = the perk id (an item_modifier tagged auPerk).
  A part is a QUALITY item (1-90): the tiered effect group below is what gives an item a quality (ItemClass.HasQuality =
  the item has a tiered effect group; its single passive is a zero, so it changes nothing). The perk a part adds runs at
  the part's quality. Parts never stack (Stacknumber 1) and show the quality bar (ShowQuality).
    - Crafted at the Gunsmith Bench (recipes.xml / the UL add-on): always quality 1 (src/CraftQuality.cs).
    - Looted: quality from the container's loot quality template, like any other loot.
    - Upgraded at Undead Legacy's Maintenance Station: MaintenanceGroup MG_auPerkPart / MG_auCorruptPart (UL add-on recipes.xml).
    - A Repair Kit at the bench takes a perk off a gun and gives this part back at the perk's quality.
  Corrupted parts (Tags auCorruptPart) have no recipe: loot only (hardened chests T4/T5, group auCorruptParts).
  To add a part for your own perk: copy a block, rename it auPart<Name>, set AuPerk, add auPart<Name> and auPart<Name>Desc to Localization.txt.
  Generated by tools/gen_parts.py.
-->
